      "description": "Underground Mortuary provides B/G mana, colors GPT4om Valley already has abundant access to (2x Overgrown Tomb + Forest for G, 2x Overgrown Tomb for B). Hedge Maze would provide a second blue source (currently only Breeding Pool), which is important for casting cards like Deceit (which needs UU for the bounce mode) or other blue spells they might draw.",
      "action_taken": "Fetched Underground Mortuary (B/G dual)",
      "better_line": "Fetch Hedge Maze (G/U dual) to shore up the weakest color in their mana base, giving a second blue source for potential blue-heavy spells.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 67,
      "player": "GPT4om Valley",
      "decision_index": 64,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "GPT4om Valley forestcycled Generous Ent to find a Forest when they already had Misty Rainforest in hand that could fetch a Forest. This wastes a 5/7 reach creature that could have been hard-cast next turn with 6 mana (after playing and cracking Misty Rainforest). Instead they end up with 7 lands and no threats in hand.",
      "action_taken": "Forestcycled Generous Ent to search for a Forest, leaving only Misty Rainforest in hand with no spells.",
      "better_line": "Play Misty Rainforest, crack it for a land (reaching 6 mana), then cast Generous Ent next turn as a 5/7 reach creature with a Food token, providing a meaningful threat and board presence against Psychic Frog.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 77,
      "player": "GPT4om Valley",
      "decision_index": 72,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Hedge Maze (which enters tapped) instead of Misty Rainforest (which can immediately crack for an untapped land) means GPT4om Valley has less mana available this turn. Misty Rainforest would provide an untapped land immediately, giving access to more mana for potential plays or responses. Hedge Maze enters tapped and provides no mana this turn. While the surveil 1 from Hedge Maze has some value, the tempo loss of playing a tapped land over a fetchland is suboptimal, especially when facing an opponent's Psychic Frog that could grow and threaten. Additionally, saving the Hedge Maze for a later turn when tempo matters less would have been better sequencing.",
      "action_taken": "Played Hedge Maze (enters tapped) as their land for the turn.",
      "better_line": "Play Misty Rainforest, crack it for an untapped dual land to have more mana available this turn for interaction, and save Hedge Maze for a turn where the tempo loss matters less.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 79,
      "player": "GPT4om Valley",
      "decision_index": 79,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Chump-blocking with Psychic Frog trades away a key threat that generates card advantage (draws on combat damage, grows with discards) for minimal value. The Frog dies without killing anything since Endurance is 3/4. At 15 life, taking the combat damage is affordable.",
      "action_taken": "Blocked with Psychic Frog, losing it in combat without trading for anything",
      "better_line": "Take the combat damage (likely ~5 points) and keep Psychic Frog alive to attack next turn, potentially growing it and drawing cards. They have Bitter Triumph in hand to deal with threats if needed, and another Psychic Frog in hand as backup.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 82,
      "player": "Qwen3 Vorthos",
      "decision_index": 84,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Formidable Speaker's activated ability '{1}, {T}: Untap another target permanent' was used to untap Ragavan, Nimble Pilferer — an opponent's creature. This gives the opponent's Ragavan the ability to block when it otherwise would have been tapped, or simply provides no benefit to GPT4om Valley. Untapping an opponent's creature is actively detrimental. GPT4om Valley should have untapped one of their own tapped lands (like Underground Mortuary which was tapped) to generate additional mana, or simply untapped one of their own permanents for value.",
      "action_taken": "Used Formidable Speaker's untap ability targeting opponent's Ragavan, Nimble Pilferer",
