      "decision_index": 94,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "GPT4om Valley cast Shardless Agent before playing Misty Rainforest from hand. Playing the land first is strictly better sequencing: it ensures the land drop isn't missed, and more importantly, sacrificing Misty Rainforest before casting Shardless Agent would enable Revolt for any Fatal Push that might be cascaded into (though that's not in their deck). Additionally, cracking a fetchland before cascade lets you shuffle away unwanted top cards and thin the deck slightly, marginally improving cascade hits. There's also the consideration that if Shardless Agent cascades into something that requires mana, having an extra land in play could matter. Playing land before spells is a fundamental sequencing principle.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Shardless Agent before playing Misty Rainforest",
