      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 128,
      "player": "Qwen3 Vorthos",
      "decision_index": 152,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Qwen3 Vorthos chose to Persist back Psychic Frog (a 1/2 that becomes 0/1 with the -1/-1 counter) instead of Abhorrent Oculus (a 5/5 flyer that becomes 4/4 with the counter and generates manifest dread tokens every opponent's upkeep). The graveyard has 13 cards, well more than the 6 needed for Oculus's additional cost (which only applies when casting, not when put onto the battlefield via Persist). At 7 life facing an opponent with Formidable Speaker and Endurance (both tapped), Abhorrent Oculus as a 4/4 flyer would be a massive threat that dominates the board and generates card advantage every turn. Psychic Frog as a 0/1 is nearly useless — it needs discard fuel to grow and the hand is now empty after casting Persist.",
