      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 131,
      "player": "Qwen3 Vorthos",
      "decision_index": 157,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Formidable Speaker's activated ability ({1}, {T}: Untap another target permanent) was used to target Deceit, which is in the graveyard, not on the battlefield. This appears to be a misunderstanding of the board state - Deceit is listed in the graveyard, not as a permanent on the battlefield. The player wasted Formidable Speaker's tap ability (preventing it from attacking) to untap something that likely doesn't exist as a valid target. Meanwhile, with the opponent at 7 life and having creatures that could attack, tapping Formidable Speaker for no meaningful benefit is costly. The player should have either attacked with Formidable Speaker or used the untap ability on one of their own tapped lands to have mana available.",
